{"event_type":"review","id":"1829a6c8fe9f70ca71d78b13e4b77a255990ff6a46bad20d812bfe26d1c50487","occurred_at":"2026-11-18T03:12:25Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/645d6734a83853fbbbdedc87b46d11589c954061d130700dacb94dc3deab7c44","sha256":"645d6734a83853fbbbdedc87b46d11589c954061d130700dacb94dc3deab7c44"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c99cddff3b4bc752b8b74aab82f01dd359d1ed6eccb5a324901e557a7cb383b2","sha256":"c99cddff3b4bc752b8b74aab82f01dd359d1ed6eccb5a324901e557a7cb383b2"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5e3c2bbaf88f0ae2ea1487fab6dbc60b8e5f43c2e43e1262d7b840ebb8f824f3","sha256":"5e3c2bbaf88f0ae2ea1487fab6dbc60b8e5f43c2e43e1262d7b840ebb8f824f3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/54379b61134d5568821f004f62dda86ecdae0a4854c30f4bf0493b183fee0950","sha256":"54379b61134d5568821f004f62dda86ecdae0a4854c30f4bf0493b183fee0950"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/da9847aaf5d53d09a75b645ec8a0b2c0cb9cfb752535f8d434c399345e4ac359","sha256":"da9847aaf5d53d09a75b645ec8a0b2c0cb9cfb752535f8d434c399345e4ac359"}],"attempt_id":"53706677a1414986ea26d8f13ae1aec85616abeab544a89941da599bf28645ed:0:1","base":"9a78dbd2edf423c3b26a8c637212b545ba3b9832","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"fcbd010882f3acd48bd6e00fbf746fa43a596d87","body":"**Close the quoted argument list in `timeoutDetail`.**\n\n`timeoutDetail` omits the closing quote of the final argument. For `['gh', 'api', 'user']`, it returns `Command '['gh', 'api', 'user]' timed out after 60 seconds`. Python's `TimeoutExpired` message is `Command '['gh', 'api', 'user']' timed out after 60 seconds`. The file states that scripted timeouts must preserve the oracle's exception details. When this message reaches the compared error text, timeout vectors fail the exact message check.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  return `Command '['${argv.join(\"', '\")}]' timed out after 60 seconds`;\n+  return `Command '['${argv.join(\"', '\")}']' timed out after 60 seconds`;\n```\n\n</details>","id":"77850856c7113e6a2891965ee548c62771b0c74d54f6236a43c7cf550a29fe6c","intervals":[[288,288]],"path":"test/policy/crq/prReviewFindings.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Close the quoted argument list in `timeoutDetail`."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"dafa6e739461f6e0594697b44f5c703be1bb565d","body":"**Stop overwriting the replayed titles before the byte comparison.**\n\nThe replay copies each expected title into the `publishSummary` result before it compares bytes. Any title the implementation returns is replaced first, so a wrong cached or fetched title still matches the fixture when the `gh` call log is unchanged. Remove the copy loop. Pass the recorded `gh` title responses through `ghTitle`, so the byte comparison checks titles that the implementation produced.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Required behavior</summary>\n\nCompare the unmodified `publishSummary` output with the fixture bytes. The `gh` stub must return the recorded title responses. The fixture's `gh_calls` content was not inspected, so the exact response format needed by the stub is not established here.\n\n</details>","id":"f1d0b22f45c583c047e34bba76c784b4e287174c06290e36c2f0f64fa5a7916b","intervals":[[333,333]],"path":"test/policy/crq/summaryPublish.test.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Stop overwriting the replayed titles before the byte comparison."}],"head":"de9340adc65c1cbb5fd5e8139468d39d65c65bde","head_tree":"7e3bc6040d8da1acb2564424b853efe795537180","input_scope":[{"blob":"368e9c37b12dc4c2b5b220d5f3aec5f741bf829b","intervals":[[1,379]],"path":"test/policy/crq/coverageUtilization.test.ts"},{"blob":"fcbd010882f3acd